<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea Shipping - Steel scrap cargoes - March 26.</title>
<headline>S.Korea Shipping - Steel scrap cargoes - March 26.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is the arrival schedule for major steel scrap vessels unloading at South Korean ports of Inchon, Pusan, Masan, Pohang, Kwangyang and Asan, as detailed on Wednesday by South Korean surveyors.</p>
<p>Steel scrap cargoes</p>
<p>-- INCHON PORT</p>
<p> VESSEL	    TONNE    ETA	 ETD	  BUYER</p>
<p> Baltic Trident  52,000   Mar 22		   Inchon</p>
<p> Jade Orient     26,000   Mar 27		   Inchon</p>
<p>-- PUSAN PORT</p>
<p> Cargo Endurance 39,311   Mar 17    Apr 6	Dongkuk</p>
<p>-- MASAN PORT</p>
<p> Jade Pacific    28,000   Mar 16    Mar 28     Kisco</p>
<p>-- POHANG PORT</p>
<p> Fruition	  30,000   Mar 14    Mar 30     POSCO</p>
<p> Xing Su Hai     22,000   Mar 28    Apr 12     Kangwon</p>
<p> Johan-L	   30,000   Apr 10    Apr 25     POSCO</p>
<p> T.B.N	     30,000   Apr 15    Apr 30     POSCO</p>
<p>-- KWANGYANG PORT</p>
<p>No vessel calling schedule as yet</p>
<p>-- ASAN PORT</p>
<p> Sea Glory	 27,703   Mar 18    Mar 28     Hanbo</p>
<p> Kalma	     31,263   Mar 20    Mar 31     Hanbo</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
